WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.723
The method has two halves.

00:00:01.803 --> 00:00:03.179
First, data curation.

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:09.211
GeoReasoner introduces a locatability metric:
MaskFormer segments each street view into

00:00:09.291 --> 00:00:11.430
semantic classes like buildings,

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.105
sky, and vehicles, producing a vector of area ratios.

00:00:15.185 --> 00:00:21.831
Sentence-BERT then measures how relevant each class
is to the textual clues mined from geo-games,

00:00:21.911 --> 00:00:23.634
producing a weight vector.

00:00:23.714 --> 00:00:31.192
The locatability of an image is simply the weighted
sum of its class ratios against these importance weights,

00:00:31.272 --> 00:00:35.699
and images scoring above a threshold of zero point
four are kept.

00:00:35.779 --> 00:00:42.633
This filters over one hundred thirty thousand raw
images down to seventy thousand high-quality ones.

00:00:42.713 --> 00:00:43.881
Second, the model.

00:00:43.961 --> 00:00:48.457
Built on Qwen-VL with a vision encoder, a
vision-language adapter,

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:50.745
and a pre-trained language model,

00:00:50.825 --> 00:00:57.055
GeoReasoner is fine-tuned in two stages using
lightweight LoRA adapters: a reasoning-tuning

00:00:57.135 --> 00:01:01.285
stage that learns country-level explanations from
game clues,

00:01:01.365 --> 00:01:08.080
followed by a location-tuning stage that sharpens
city-level accuracy on the curated street views.
